\f0\b\fs36 \cf2 Part 1: Pre-Build Checklist\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa320\partightenfactor0

\f1\b0\fs24 \cf2 \
Completing these preparation steps correctly is critical and will prevent most common submission errors.\
\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa160\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs28 \cf2 1.1 Update Version and Build Numbers\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa320\partightenfactor0

\f1\b0\fs24 \cf2 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa160\partightenfactor0
\cf2 The \cf4 \cb5 \strokec4 pubspec.yaml\cf2 \cb1 \strokec2  file is the single source of truth for versioning. Apple requires every new submission to have a higher version and/or build number.\
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\sa160\partightenfactor0
\ls1\ilvl0\cf2 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	1	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Open the \cf4 \cb5 \strokec4 pubspec.yaml\cf2 \cb1 \strokec2  file in the project's root directory.\
\ls1\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	2	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Locate the \cf4 \cb5 \strokec4 version:\cf2 \cb1 \strokec2  line. It follows the format \cf4 \cb5 \strokec4 version: [version_name]+[build_number]\cf2 \cb1 \strokec2 .\
\pard\tx940\tx1440\pardeftab720\li1440\fi-1440\sa160\partightenfactor0
\ls1\ilvl1
\f0\b \cf2 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	
\f2 \uc0\u9702 
\f0 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Version Name (e.g., \cf4 \cb5 \strokec4 1.0.11\cf2 \cb1 \strokec2 ):
\f1\b0  This is the public-facing version on the App Store. It must be equal to or higher than the current live version.\
\ls1\ilvl1
\f0\b \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	
\f2 \uc0\u9702 
\f0 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Build Number (e.g., \cf4 \cb5 \strokec4 +24\cf2 \cb1 \strokec2 ):
\f1\b0  This is an internal number. It 
\f0\b must be strictly higher
\f1\b0  than the last build number uploaded to App Store Connect.\
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\sa160\partightenfactor0
\ls1\ilvl0\cf2 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	3	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Increment the numbers as needed and save the file.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa320\partightenfactor0
\cf2 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa160\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs28 \cf2 1.2 Verify Apple Developer Account in Xcode\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa320\partightenfactor0

\f1\b0\fs24 \cf2 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa160\partightenfactor0
\cf2 The project must be signed by the official paid Apple Developer account that owns the app.\
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\sa160\partightenfactor0
\ls2\ilvl0\cf2 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	1	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 In Xcode, navigate to the menu bar: 
\f0\b Xcode > Settings... > Accounts
\f1\b0 .\
\ls2\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	2	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Ensure that the correct Apple ID for the 
\f0\b University of Hyderabad
\f1\b0  developer program is signed in.\
\ls2\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	3	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Remove any other personal or incorrect accounts to avoid conflicts.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa320\partightenfactor0
\cf2 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa160\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs28 \cf2 1.3 Verify Project Team Selection\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa320\partightenfactor0

\f1\b0\fs24 \cf2 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa160\partightenfactor0
\cf2 The Xcode project itself must be assigned to the correct team.\
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\sa160\partightenfactor0
\ls3\ilvl0\cf2 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	1	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Open the iOS module by running \cf4 \cb5 \strokec4 open ios/Runner.xcworkspace\cf2 \cb1 \strokec2  in the terminal.\
\ls3\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	2	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Select the 
\f0\b Runner
\f1\b0  target, then navigate to the 
\f0\b Signing & Capabilities
\f1\b0  tab.\
\ls3\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	3	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 In the 
\f0\b Team
\f1\b0  dropdown menu, ensure the official paid team (
\f0\b University of Hyderabad
\f1\b0 ) is selected, not a "Personal Team".\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf3 \strokec3 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa320\partightenfactor0
\cf2 \strokec2 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa160\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs36 \cf2 Part 2: Creating the iOS App Archive\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa320\partightenfactor0

\f1\b0\fs24 \cf2 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa160\partightenfactor0
\cf2 This process packages the app into a format required by the App Store.\
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\sa160\partightenfactor0
\ls4\ilvl0\cf2 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	1	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 In the top bar of Xcode, set the build destination to 
\f0\b Any iOS Device (arm64)
\f1\b0 .\
\ls4\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	2	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 From the top menu bar, select 
\f0\b Product > Archive
\f1\b0 .\
\ls4\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	3	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Xcode will build the project. This may take several minutes.\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf3 \strokec3 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa320\partightenfactor0
\cf2 \strokec2 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa160\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs36 \cf2 Part 3: Uploading the Build to App Store Connect\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa320\partightenfactor0

\f1\b0\fs24 \cf2 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa160\partightenfactor0
\cf2 When the archive is successfully created, the Xcode Organizer window will appear.\
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\sa160\partightenfactor0
\ls5\ilvl0\cf2 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	1	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Select the new archive from the list on the left (verify it has the correct version and build number).\
\ls5\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	2	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Click the blue 
\f0\b "Distribute App"
\f1\b0  button.\
\ls5\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	3	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 In the wizard, select the following options:\
\pard\tx940\tx1440\pardeftab720\li1440\fi-1440\sa160\partightenfactor0
\ls5\ilvl1\cf2 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	
\f3 \uc0\u9702 
\f1 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Method: 
\f0\b App Store Connect
\f1\b0 \
\ls5\ilvl1\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	
\f3 \uc0\u9702 
\f1 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Destination: 
\f0\b Upload
\f1\b0 \
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\sa160\partightenfactor0
\ls5\ilvl0\cf2 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	4	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Proceed through the remaining steps, confirming signing details. Once you click 
\f0\b Upload
\f1\b0 , Xcode will send the build to Apple's servers.\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf3 \strokec3 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa320\partightenfactor0
\cf2 \strokec2 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa160\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs36 \cf2 Part 4: Submitting the Update for Review\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa320\partightenfactor0

\f1\b0\fs24 \cf2 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa160\partightenfactor0
\cf2 The final steps are performed on the App Store Connect website after you receive an email confirming your build has finished processing.\
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\sa160\partightenfactor0
\ls6\ilvl0\cf2 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	1	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Go to 
\f0\b \cf4 \cb5 \strokec4 appstoreconnect.apple.com
\f1\b0 \cf2 \cb1 \strokec2 , sign in, and select the Samsaadhanii app.\
\ls6\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	2	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Navigate to the 
\f0\b App Store
\f1\b0  tab.\
\ls6\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	3	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Click the 
\f0\b plus (\cf4 \cb5 \strokec4 +\cf2 \cb1 \strokec2 ) button
\f1\b0  in the left sidebar to create a new version. Enter the version number that matches your \cf4 \cb5 \strokec4 pubspec.yaml\cf2 \cb1 \strokec2  file (e.g., \cf4 \cb5 \strokec4 1.0.11\cf2 \cb1 \strokec2 ).\
\ls6\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	4	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Fill out the required information on the submission page:\
\pard\tx940\tx1440\pardeftab720\li1440\fi-1440\sa160\partightenfactor0
\ls6\ilvl1
\f0\b \cf2 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	
\f2 \uc0\u9702 
\f0 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 What's New in This Version:
\f1\b0  Enter your release notes.\
\ls6\ilvl1
\f0\b \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	
\f2 \uc0\u9702 
\f0 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Screenshots:
\f1\b0  Update these if the app's UI has changed.\
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\sa160\partightenfactor0
\ls6\ilvl0\cf2 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	5	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Scroll to the 
\f0\b "Build"
\f1\b0  section and click the plus (\cf4 \cb5 \strokec4 +\cf2 \cb1 \strokec2 ) button to select the build you just uploaded.\
\ls6\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	6	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Once all information is complete, click 
\f0\b "Add for Review"
\f1\b0  in the top-right corner, followed by 
\f0\b "Submit to App Review"
\f1\b0 .\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
